nodes.body:
@mickqian Could you please reopen this MiMo-VL PR for review? It was closed by the idle-PR cleanup. This is a one-line call-site change that reuses the existing `permute_inv` helper to construct the inverse window permutation directly; current `main` still sorts it with `torch.argsort`.

The earlier H200 validation found bit-exact parity for eight image/video/mixed-grid cases on each of eight GPUs, and the MiMo-V2.5 TP8/DP2/FA3 two-image integration request passed. Inverse-construction latency fell by 37.3%–79.6% across the measured sizes. Those are component measurements; there is no model-level end-to-end speedup claim.

I would like to continue review of this small change. Could you reopen it, or help route it to the MiMo/vision reviewer? I can rebase and rerun the checks for the updated head as needed. Thanks!

